# The trial of pod-hostprobe in podvm (T-055): crates/podvm-probe keeps its
# report, exit codes, JSON writer and non-goals, and re-exports the modules of
# pod-hostprobe (sys, child, verdict, probes, select, identity, interp,
# machine, mounts, binfmt, writable, supervise), so each user of
# `podvm_probe::X` in podvm keeps its path. podvm-probe gives podvm's
# Settings (`--probe-child`, `podvm`, `$PODVM_STORE`), reads PODVM_STORE and
# writable::VARIABLES for the write probe, and gives the emulator check the
# variables of the process. select.rs keeps BANNER_ROWS and banner_cell.
# podvm-image's space.rs and exec_probe.rs call pod-hostprobe with podvm's
# settings and map its pod_core::Failure to podvm's errors (no space:
# NoSpace; a path with a NUL: Store; an I/O failure: Io). The 26 moved files
# leave podvm; each podcrates tag moves to v0.6.0. The wire line is
# `pod-hostprobe/1`.
# podvm's tests of each touched crate and each user of podvm-probe; the
# probe children through the binary (`podvm probe --rows`: 66 rows, each
# child gives a line that the parent reads); clippy of the workspace and
# rustfmt of the touched crates, as podvm's gate.yml runs them; the
# runtime-state rows; podvm's record gate; each Rust toolchain of the
# workflows against the rust-version of podcrates; and the binaries `node`
# and `podvm` for x86_64 musl, with podcrates' static check.
cargo test -q -p podvm-probe
cargo test -q -p podvm-image
# resolve_past_a_denied_listing runs the test binary as the user nobody. It
# cannot do that where the target directory is under a home of mode 0700, and
# it does not touch the probes.
cargo test -q -p podvm-enter -- --skip abi::tests::resolve_past_a_denied_listing
cargo test -q -p podvm-extract
cargo test -q -p podvm-supervise
cargo test -q -p podvm-windows
cargo test -q -p podvm-complete --lib
cargo test -q -p podvm-ssh --lib
cargo test -q -p podvm-release
cargo test -q -p podvm --bin podvm
cargo test -q -p podvm --test store_gates
if command -v sshd > /dev/null || [ -x /usr/sbin/sshd ]; then cargo test -q -p podvm-ssh --test mux_two_client; else echo "adoption: no sshd: the test mux_two_client does not run"; fi
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -p podvm-probe -p podvm-image -p podvm-gate -p podvm-release --check
# The probe children: the binary starts itself with --probe-child for each
# probe. A child line that the parent cannot read is a skip that names "the
# child for".
cargo build -q -p podvm-ssh --bin node && cargo build -q -p podvm --bin podvm
"${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm" --probe-child 'chroot(/tmp)' | grep -q '^pod-hostprobe/1 verdict='
mkdir -p target && "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm" probe --rows > target/probe-rows.txt; test "$(wc -l < target/probe-rows.txt)" -eq 66 && ! grep -q 'the child for' target/probe-rows.txt
# podvm's gate finds the root of the repository from the path of its binary,
# so it runs from target/release/, with document-state beside it (gate.yml).
cargo build -q --release -p podvm-gate && cargo build -q --release -p podvm-release --bin document-state
mkdir -p target/release && cp "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/podvm-gate" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/document-state" target/release/
# docs/runtime-state.md lists each direct git or registry dependency with its
# locked version. The patch gives the rows of the git form (pod-core,
# pod-hostprobe, pod-proxy, pod-term and pod-tls at 0.6.0); the trial's path
# form has no row for them. Each other row of the patch must be the generated
# one: linux-raw-sys leaves, and Rung is named in pod-hostprobe.
grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md > target/runtime-state.patch.md && python3 scripts/document-state.py --write && grep -v '^| .pod-' docs/runtime-state.md | diff target/runtime-state.patch.md -
./target/release/podvm-gate
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/node"
sh "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-static.sh" "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podvm"
